// TDShop settings, rendered by the base Einstellungen host via
// virtual:frontend-settings.
//
// Checkpoint 1 has nothing to configure: the catalogue needs no credentials.
// The Amazon Product Advertising keys and the Stripe keys arrive with their own
// checkpoints and land here, read through the core SettingsStore (namespace
// `shop`) and encrypted with SETTINGS_ENCRYPTION_KEY — never in .env, and never
// in a PUBLIC_ variable.
---

<div class="tds-settings-section__body">
  <p>
    Der Katalog braucht keine Zugangsdaten. Die Schlüssel für den
    Amazon-Angebotsabgleich und für Stripe erscheinen hier, sobald die
    jeweiligen Funktionen ausgeliefert sind.
  </p>
</div>
